       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5,000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day, nearly four times the usual maximum adult acetaminophen dose of 4 g/day. At that dose, even with normal liver function, there is a serious risk of acute hepatotoxicity and liver failure. A 70 kg patient with normal kidney and liver function and no allergies doesn't change that.\n\nWas this a typo? Some common options are:\n- **500 mg PO three times daily** (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily** (4 g/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 5,000 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'd want to put that in the order note, and it may also need pharmacy review."
